  "report_period": "Week 3 (12th Jan to 19th Jan 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Eagle Bulk Shipping have committed their Supramax \"Crested Eagle\" & \"Stellar Eagle\" 56/2009 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 04/2024 & SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) at USD 14,5 mill each, while the \"Queen Kobe\" 55/2009 Kawasaki, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold to Indonesian buyers at high USD 14 mill. Remind you that in early December, the one- year-older \"Ermione\" 56/2008 IHI, Japan (SS 09/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 14,2 mill. In addition, the \"APJ Jad\" 52/2002 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 05/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) from Apeejay Shipping was committed at USD 7,2 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Star Theta\" 52/2003 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 06/2028, DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,5 mill. The Handysize \"Alam Suria\" 29/2012 Shikoku, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) of Tsurumi Kisen was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 11,8 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"Agali\" 28/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2028, DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold three weeks ago at low USD 13 mill.",
    "tankers": "Angelicoussis Shipping committed their VLCC \"Elizabeth I.A.\" 306/2004 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 34 mill. Remind you that the Japanese built \"Jessica D\" 301/2004 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024) was sold in late November at USD 32,5 mill. On the Aframax sector, Active Shipping committed the \"Fair Seas\" 115/2008 Stx, Korea (SS 07/2028, DD 09/2026) for USD 43,5 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-older \"Aegean Power\" 115/2007 Samsung, Korea (SS 04/2027, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 42 mill. Harren Tanker Management have commited the LR1 \"Pataris \"73/2009 New Times, China (SS/DD 04/2024, BWTS fitted) to clients of Trafigura at USD 26 mill, while the two-year-older Korean built \"Brook Trout\" & \"Lake Trout\" 73/2007 Stx, Korea (SS 08/2027, DD 12/2025 & SS 07/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1A) of Prime Marine Management were committed to Emarat Maritime at USD 26 mill each also. The MR1 \"Dinah\" & \"Pluto\" 37/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 11/2028, DD 12/2025 & SS 10/2028, DD 11/2028, Ice Class A1) were committed at USD 41,75 mill enbloc. For reference, the two-years-older \"Baltic Freedom\" 37/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 09/2026, DD 10/2024, Ice Class 1A) was sold back in September at region USD 18 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 7,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 9,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 7,000/10,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/17,000 pd. West African trips via US Gulf into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 26,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast and South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 24,000/26,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K/900K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 15,000 pd for 8/10 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the level of usd 8,000/9,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K/219K. Continental trips via Baltic into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 19,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. An Ultramax was fixed on a period at the usd 14,500 pd basis delivery China for 11/13 months employment.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 18,000 pd. South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
